Creation: nriCreateDevice with no adapter desc probes only the Vulkan backend for a Vulkan device.

nriEnumerateAdapters takes the backends to probe since 962615b (#286), but nriCreateDevice with a
null "adapterDesc" still calls it with every backend: creating a VK device creates a DXGI factory
and D3D12 devices and leaves D3D12Core.dll loaded for the process's life (an overlay then labels
the process D3D12 until a VK swap chain appears). The D3D pass only adds D3D bits to an adapter the
VK pass listed, so a VK-only probe lists the same VK adapters with the same descs, in the same
order; a device of any other API keeps the full probe, because when both passes list an adapter
its desc (queue counts, memory sizes) is the VK pass's, and a D3D-only probe would change it.

This passes GraphicsAPI::VK for a VK device and GraphicsAPI::ALL otherwise, two lines. The same
rule as master's 0024 (nriEnumerateAdapters2 on v190), which #286 made unnecessary on main.
Measured on v190 with master's 0024, NVIDIA RTX 4070 SUPER: a VK-only enumeration took 67.0 ms the
first call and 5.3 ms the second and left D3D12Core.dll unloaded, as did creating a Vulkan device
with no adapter afterwards (104.5 ms); an unfiltered enumeration took 125.1 ms and 69.1 ms and
loaded D3D12Core.dll.

diff --git a/Source/Creation/Creation.cpp b/Source/Creation/Creation.cpp
index e6e71b63..20187fbc 100644
--- a/Source/Creation/Creation.cpp
+++ b/Source/Creation/Creation.cpp
@@ -915,7 +915,9 @@ NRI_API Result NRI_CALL nriCreateDevice(const DeviceCreationDesc& deviceCreation
     std::array<AdapterDesc, ADAPTER_MAX_NUM> adapterDescs = {};
     AdapterDesc adapterDesc = {};
     if (!modifiedDeviceCreationDesc.adapterDesc) {
-        nriEnumerateAdapters(adapterDescs.data(), adapterDescNum);
+        // A VK device needs the VK pass only; the D3D pass would create D3D12 devices and keep "D3D12Core.dll" loaded. A D3D12 adapter desc depends on the VK pass (queue counts), so other APIs probe everything
+        GraphicsAPI desiredGraphicsAPIs = modifiedDeviceCreationDesc.graphicsAPI == GraphicsAPI::VK ? GraphicsAPI::VK : GraphicsAPI::ALL;
+        nriEnumerateAdapters(adapterDescs.data(), adapterDescNum, desiredGraphicsAPIs);
         for (uint32_t i = 0; i < adapterDescNum; i++) {
             if (adapterDescs[i].supportedGraphicsAPIs & modifiedDeviceCreationDesc.graphicsAPI) {
                 adapterDesc = adapterDescs[i];
